<!-- The guild tab of the group window (TSe_TeamForm with its guild tab chosen); view model:
     viewmodels/GuildWindow.cpp.  The game keeps one form and swaps its picture; here the guild
     tab is a window of its own that opens where the group window was.  Its four pages:
     Guild Info (the lord, how many members, the rules with End Guild and Edit Rule for the lord),
     Member (five a page: face, name, level, job, element, state, nickname and title, a mail icon
     and a tick box, with the buttons that act on the ticked ones), Insignia and Message.  The
     game draws a form's controls from the last created to the first: the controls here are in
     drawing order, the reverse of TSe_TeamForm.Create.  The Message page (the guild's notice
     board) is in viewmodels/GuildNoticePage.cpp, the Insignia page (the badge editor) in
     viewmodels/GuildEmblemPage.cpp. -->
